<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vilnius University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> University is the oldest university in the Baltic states, founded in 1579 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> Báthory raised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> college of Vilnius to the rank of an academy. It became the main centre of learning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. Closed by the Russian authorities in 1832 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/november-uprising">November Uprising</a>, it reopened in 1919 and remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>'s leading university.</p></div>
